window.docContents[165].resolve({"/Calculational-proofs/#calculational-proofs":{"contents":"In Mathlib, proofs by calculation whose steps are equalities of kernels are rare. Each of their structural steps is a chain of rewritings, which buries the meaningful steps. Such steps are, e.g., reassociating a composition, marginalizing an output or moving a kernel along a copy. With Kernel-Hom, the structural steps are proved by kernel_disch, in the same way as cat_disch or monoidal proves the easy steps of categorical proofs. Thus, a proof can be written as a calc whose lines are the meaningful rewrites. With measure_kernel, this also holds for calculations on measures built from kernels. On paper, the structural steps are invisible. Indeed, they relate string diagrams that only differ by a deformation of the wires or by the axioms of copy-discard categories.\n\n\n\n","context":"Kernel-Hom: Tactics for Kernel Categorical Reasoning","header":"2. Calculational proofs","id":"/Calculational-proofs/#calculational-proofs"}});